-- The integrally scaled vacuum θ° = κ₀ⁿ·vac of a standard space and the
-- module of standard data at a p-adic place: the scaled vacuum has
-- integral values with bounded conjugates, and some value is nonzero.
-- Source: grh-compact/src/New/Curve/IntegralVacuum.lean ("This file:
-- Integrally scaled vacuum and the module of standard data at p. Scaled
-- vacuum has integral values with bounded conjugates; some value is
-- non-zero."; Parameters.vacuumScale, kappa₀_ne_zero,
-- Parameters.intVacuum, Parameters.integralAfter,
-- Parameters.standardData, norm_intVacuum_le, norm_intVacuum_le_one,
-- exists_intVacuum_ne_zero).
-- Encoding. The source chooses κ₀ (Parameters.vacuumScale) as the number
-- c of exists_isJetConjugate_generator at the standard space of rank one;
-- here κ₀ is an argument k bound by VacuumScaleOf, the property it is
-- chosen by (VacuumScaleAt at every standard space of rank one, for the
-- constant C of JetConjugateBound). A finite adelic vector x is a point of
-- spacePoints(V), its coordinates finite adeles, and the value
-- θ°(finVec x) is θ(ϱ(αx)θ°) = κ₀ⁿ vac(x). Standard data, the least
-- ι⁻¹𝔬-submodule with the stated closure, is the intersection of all such
-- submodules. Not stated here: isAdmissibleComb_name (admissible
-- combinations and moduli of New/Seesaw), intVacuum_finVec_eq_prod (the
-- product formula over the rank-one space) and norm_dataInner_le.
-- Part of the GRH blueprint (layer 5, the argument).
